TITLE:: MENote
summary:: MENote object for MENoteRange
categories:: MusicEngine Library
related:: Classes/MENoteRange, Classes/MERange

DESCRIPTION::
CODE::MENote:: encapsulates all note data (midi, frequency, degree, name, etc.) into a single object.
NOTE:: CODE::MENote:: objects were not designed to be instantiated directly by the user, but to be instantiated internally when generating a CODE::MENoteRange::. The user may then access them, via the CODE::MENoteRange:: object, and retrieve data using the methods described in this file.

CODE::
~r = MENoteRange("F#-7"); // MENoteRange[C#-1:P5, E-1:m7, F#-1:P1, A-1:m3, ...]
~r.size;      // A 43 MENote collection, ranging from octaves -1 to 9
~r[30].name   // F#6
~r[30].midi   // 90
~r[30].degree // P1
::
::


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new

ARGUMENT:: noteLetter
Letter to be used when generating a note name.

ARGUMENT:: midiNote
MIDI note number.

ARGUMENT:: interval
Note degree in relation to a root.

ARGUMENT:: data
User defined data Dictionary. If none is provided, an empty dictionary will be assigned to the new CODE::MENote:: object.

ARGUMENT:: validate
Used for debugging only. When set to CODE::true::, validate activates validator methods that test input validity throughout the process of creating a CODE::MENote:: instance.

returns:: A new CODE::MENote:: object.



METHOD:: newFromName

ARGUMENT:: noteName
String representing the note name (e.g., EMPHASIS::C#4::). String must contain letter (EMPHASIS::A-G::), zero to 5 sharps or flats, and octave number.

ARGUMENT:: interval
Degree to be associated with the note. Should be of type CODE::Symbol::.

ARGUMENT:: data
User defined data Dictionary. If none is provided, an empty dictionary will be assigned to the new CODE::MENote:: object.

returns:: A new CODE::MENote:: object


INSTANCEMETHODS::



SUBSECTION:: Pitch data



METHOD:: midi

returns:: The MIDI note number.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].midi; // 30
::



METHOD:: freq

returns:: The frequency value.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].freq; // 46.249302838954
::



SUBSECTION:: Name data



METHOD:: name

ARGUMENT:: charSet
Character set to be used on the accidental sign. Options are: CODE::\ascii::, for ASCII characters; CODE::\unic::, for Unicode characters and CODE::\m21::, for a format compatible with the Python's module STRONG::music21::.

ARGUMENT:: withOctave
Whether octave number should be appended at the end.

returns:: A String representing the note name.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].name;               // F#1
r[10].name(\unic, false); // F♯
::



METHOD:: sol
Uses the EMPHASIS::solfege:: convention when generating a note name (EMPHASIS::Do, Re, Mi, Fa, Sol, La, Si::).

ARGUMENT:: charSet
Character set to be used on the accidental sign. Options are: CODE::\ascii::, for ASCII characters; CODE::\unic::, for Unicode characters and CODE::\m21::, for a format compatible with the Python's module STRONG::music21::.


ARGUMENT:: withOctave
Whether octave number should be appended at the end.

returns:: A String representing the note name.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].sol;               // Fa#1
r[10].sol(\unic, false); // Fa♯
::



METHOD:: letter

returns:: The letter representing the note name.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].letter; // F
::



METHOD:: octave

returns:: The octave number as an integer.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].octave; // 1
::



METHOD:: sign

ARGUMENT:: charSet
Character set to be used on the accidental sign. Options are: CODE::\ascii::, for ASCII characters; CODE::\unic::, for Unicode characters and CODE::\m21::, for a format compatible with the Python's module STRONG::music21::.

returns:: The accidental sign.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].sign;        // #
r[10].sign(\unic); // ♯
::


METHOD:: signOffset
The sign offset is an integer representation of the accidental sign attributed to the note when generating a name. The offset may range from -5 (CODE::bbbbb::) to 5 (CODE::#####::). A value of 0 indicates that the note has no accidental.

returns:: The accidental sign offset as an integer.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].signOffset; // 1
::



SUBSECTION:: Interval data



METHOD:: interval

returns:: The CODE::MEInterval:: object associated with the CODE::MENote:: instance.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].interval; // MEInterval(P1)
::


METHOD:: degree
If CODE::MENote:: is instantiated via the CODE::newFromName:: method, and no degree interval symbol is passed, degree will be set to CODE::nil::. In those cases we may assign an interval directly to degree, which will then instantiate a new CODE::MEInterval:: object internally.

CODE::
n = MENote.newFromName("Bb4");
n.degree;       // nil
n.interval;     // nil
n.number;       // nil
n.quality;      // nil

n.degree = \P5;
n.degree;       // P5
n.interval;     // MEInterval(P5)
n.number;       // 5.2
n.quality;      // P
::

returns:: Whenever CODE::MENote:: has interval data CODE::.degree::  returns a CODE::Symbol:: representing the degree. Otherwise it returns CODE::nil::.


CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].degree; // P1
::


METHOD:: number
Number returns a numeric representation of the interval, where the whole part represents the interval number, and the decimal part represents the quality (EMPHASIS::0.0, 0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4::, respectively EMPHASIS::d, m, P, M, A::)

ARGUMENT:: asInt
When set to CODE::true:: returns the whole part as an CODE::Integer::.

returns:: A numeric representation of the interval.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].number;       // 1.2 (P1)
r[10].number(true); // 1
::



METHOD:: quality
Returns the quality of the interval as a CODE::Float:: (EMPHASIS::0.0, 0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4::), or as a CODE::Symbol:: (EMPHASIS::\d, \m, \P, \M, \A::). The default is CODE::Symbol::.

ARGUMENT:: asFloat
When set to CODE::true:: returns the quality as a CODE::Float::.

returns:: The quality of the interval.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].quality;       // P
r[10].quality(true); // 0.2
::


SUBSECTION:: User assigned data


METHOD:: data
Each CODE::MENote:: object has a dictionary with user assigned values. During instantiation an empty CODE::Dictionary:: is assigned in case none was passed to the constructor.

returns:: The data CODE::Dictionary:: assigned to the CODE::MENote:: object.



METHOD:: set
Allows the user to register new values in the data CODE::Dictionary::.

ARGUMENT:: key
A key for the new CODE::Dictionary:: entry.

ARGUMENT:: value
A value to be associated with the key.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].set(\dur, 0.5);
r[10].data;           // Dictionary[(\dur -> 0.5)]
::


METHOD:: get
Allows the user to retrieve data from the CODE::Dictionary:: using the respective key.

ARGUMENT:: key
A key associated with the value the user wishes to retrieve.

returns:: The value for the given key.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].set(\dur, 0.5);
r[10].get(\dur);      // 0.5
::


METHOD:: clearValue
Allows the user to clear a key value pair.

ARGUMENT:: key
The key of the entry to be cleared.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].set(\dur, 0.5);
r[10].get(\dur);        // 0.5
r[10].clearValue(\dur);
r[10].get(\dur);        // nil
::



METHOD:: clearDict
Allows the user to clear all data inside the CODE::Dictionary::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].set(\dur, 0.5);
r[10].set(\amp, 0.3);
r[10].get(\dur);      // 0.5
r[10].get(\amp);      // 0.3
r[10].clearDict;
r[10].data.isEmpty;   // true
::



METHOD:: getKeys

returns:: A CODE::Set:: with all the keys in the CODE::Dictionary::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].set(\dur, 0.5);
r[10].set(\amp, 0.3);
r[10].getKeys;        // Set[amp, dur]
::



METHOD:: printData
Prints all entries in the CODE:: Dictionary::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10].set(\dur, 0.5);
r[10].set(\amp, 0.3);
r[10].printData;
::


SUBSECTION:: Note transposition

CODE::MENote:: transposition may be achieved using an integer value, or a symbol representing the interval by which the CODE::MENote:: is to be transposed. When transposed, note names are changed accordingly.

Symbols allow transpositions up to a 14th (CODE::\A1:: to CODE::\M14::), although the shift of the MIDI value does not go beyond MATH::\pm 11::. Using Symbols also allows for greater control over what the transposed note name will be.

Integers allow any leap provided the transposed MIDI value does not exceed 127. Integers default to the following intervals:

TABLE::
 ##0 || \P1
 ##1 || \m2
 ##2 || \M2
 ##3 || \m3
 ##4 || \M3
 ##5 || \P4
 ##6 || \A4
 ##7 || \P5
 ##8 || \m6
 ##9 || \M6
 ##10 || \m7
 ##11 || \M7
::



METHOD:: transposeUp
Allows for the transposition of a CODE::MENote:: upward.

ARGUMENT:: interval
An CODE::Integer:: or CODE::Symbol:: representing the interval by which the CODE::MENote:: is to be transposed.

returns:: A new CODE::MENote:: if MIDI value of the new CODE::MENote:: is less than or equal to 127. Otherwise it returns CODE::nil::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10];                      // F#1:P1
n = r[10].transposeUp(\d5); // C2:P1
m = r[10].transposeUp(6);   // B#1:P1

r[10].midi;                 // 30
n.midi;                     // 36
m.midi;                     // 36

// Transposition over an octave
o = r[10].transposeUp(24);  // Two octaves higher

r[10].midi;                 // 30
o.midi;                     // 54
::



METHOD:: transposeDown
Allows for the transposition of a CODE::MENote:: downward.

ARGUMENT:: interval
An CODE::Integer:: or CODE::Symbol:: representing the interval by which the CODE::MENote:: is to be transposed.

returns:: A new CODE::MENote:: if MIDI value of the new CODE::MENote:: is greater than or equal to 0. Otherwise it returns CODE::nil::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r[10];                        // F#1:P1
n = r[10].transposeDown(\d5); // B#0:P1
m = r[10].transposeDown(6);   // C1:P1

r[10].midi;                   // 30
n.midi;                       // 24
m.midi;                       // 24

// Transposition over an octave
o = r[10].transposeDown(24);  // Two octaves down

r[10].midi;                   // 30
o.midi;                       // 6
::



METHOD:: >>
Same as CODE::transposeUp::.

ARGUMENT:: interval
An CODE::Integer:: or CODE::Symbol:: representing the interval by which the CODE::MENote:: is to be transposed.

returns:: A new CODE::MENote:: if MIDI value of the new CODE::MENote:: is less than or equal to 127. Otherwise it returns CODE::nil::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");

r[10];            // F#1:P1
n = r[10] >> \d5; // C2:P1
m = r[10] >> 6;   // B#1:P1

r[10].midi;       // 30
n.midi;           // 36
m.midi;           // 36
::



METHOD:: <<
Same as CODE::transposeDown::.

ARGUMENT:: interval
An CODE::Integer:: or CODE::Symbol:: representing the interval by which the CODE::MENote:: is to be transposed.

returns:: A new CODE::MENote:: if MIDI value of the new CODE::MENote:: is greater than or equal to 0. Otherwise it returns CODE::nil::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");

r[10];            // F#1:P1
n = r[10] << \d5; // B#0:P1
m = r[10] << 6;   // C1:P1

r[10].midi;       // 30
n.midi;           // 24
m.midi;           // 24
::



SUBSECTION:: Other methods


METHOD:: copy

returns:: A deep copy of the object.
